    skos:definition "the commercial name for the bony matter of the tusks of the elephant, the teeth of the hippopotamus and walrus, the horn of the narwhal, &c. Elephant Ivory is the most esteemed, and that obtained in the largest quantity; our imports are nearly 500 tons a-year. Ivory is largely [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 218]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — source_taxon add: Heading enumerates elephant, sea-cow (hippopotamus) and sea-horse (walrus) teeth; cf. Simmonds 1892 s.v. IVORY. | source_taxon add: Heading enumerates elephant, sea-cow (hippopotamus) and sea-horse (walrus) teeth; cf. Simmonds 1892 s.v. IVORY. | source_taxon add: Heading enumerates elephant, sea-cow (hippopotamus) and sea-horse (walrus) teeth; cf. Simmonds 1892 s.v. IVORY."@en ;
